# Deploy to GitHub Pages after updates

This static site is hosted at **https://neversmile0825.github.io/Elect-The-Hottie/** via GitHub Pages from the `main` branch of https://github.com/NeverSMILE0825/Elect-The-Hottie.git.

## After any substantive site change

When you finish updating site files (`index.html`, `styles.css`, `script.js`, `assets/`, etc.):

1. Commit the changes (ask first only if the user has not already asked to deploy/publish; if they asked to update the live site or previously requested auto-publish, proceed).
2. Push to `origin main`.
3. Confirm GitHub Pages will rebuild from `main` `/` (no separate publish step — push is enough).
4. Tell the user the live URL: https://neversmile0825.github.io/Elect-The-Hottie/

## Auth / tooling notes

- Prefer `C:\Users\Administrator\gh-cli\bin\gh.exe` for GitHub CLI (PATH may point at a wrong npm `gh` package).
- Use account `NeverSMILE0825` (`gh auth switch -u NeverSMILE0825` if needed).
- Do not force-push unless the user explicitly asks.

## Do not

- Change Pages source away from `main` `/` without asking.
- Commit secrets or local-only junk.
